<h2 id="s3">3 · Minimal standalone example</h2>

<p>The single most important <em>usage pattern</em> in the repo: the pipeline is a
<strong>generator that yields progress events</strong>, and every front-end (GUI, CLI, your own
scripts) consumes the same stream. Here's the whole pattern in miniature:</p>

<pre><code><span class="com"># Consume the pipeline exactly like app/dashboard.py and the CLI do.</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> oil_alpha.pipeline <span class="kw">import</span> run_pipeline   <span class="com"># PYTHONPATH=src</span>

result = <span class="kw">None</span>
<span class="kw">for</span> event <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">run_pipeline</span>():          <span class="com"># yields ProgressEvent objects</span>
    <span class="com"># each event: stage, status ("start"/"ok"/"warn"/"error"), pct, message</span>
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="str">f"[{event.pct:4.0%}] {event.stage:&lt;13} {event.status:&lt;5} {event.message}"</span>)
    <span class="kw">if</span> event.stage == <span class="str">"done"</span>:          <span class="com"># final event carries the payload</span>
        result = event.payload           <span class="com"># a PipelineResult dataclass</span>

<span class="com"># Everything the study produced lives on one object:</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(result.leadlag.leader)             <span class="com"># "wti_fut" under a stable window</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(result.granger[<span class="str">"x-&gt;y"</span>].p_value)  <span class="com"># CL → XLE Granger p-value</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(result.budget.<span class="fn">total_requests</span>())  <span class="com"># API calls spent this run</span></code></pre>

<p>And the C++ side in miniature — feed a book, read the top:</p>

<pre><code><span class="com">// Flat-array book for an instrument expected to trade $99.00–$102.00.</span>
<span class="com">// ITCH prices are fixed-point: dollars × 10000.</span>
itch::OrderBookFlat book(<span class="num">990000</span>, <span class="num">1020000</span>);

book.<span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="com">/*order_ref=*/</span><span class="num">1</span>, <span class="str">'B'</span>, <span class="num">1000000</span>, <span class="num">100</span>);  <span class="com">// bid 100 sh @ $100.00</span>
book.<span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="num">2</span>, <span class="str">'S'</span>, <span class="num">1000500</span>, <span class="num">200</span>);              <span class="com">// ask 200 sh @ $100.05</span>
book.<span class="fn">execute</span>(<span class="num">1</span>, <span class="num">40</span>);                          <span class="com">// 40 shares of the bid trade</span>

<span class="kw">auto</span> sig = itch::<span class="fn">make_signal</span>(book);           <span class="com">// works for both book types</span>
<span class="com">// sig.bid_price=100.00, sig.ask_price=100.05, sig.mid=100.025, sig.valid=true</span></code></pre>

